{"title":"1973 AHSME Problems/Problem 21","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The number of sets of two or more consecutive positive integers whose sum is 100 is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/8/908080b56fc36e805bfef13f09a77a76e2624126.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 1 \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ 2 \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ 3 \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ 4 \\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"348\" height=\"17\" /> \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If the first number of a group of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> consecutive numbers is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/5/3657b37b69a5e1029f9182897c6b5dc7492cc1bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^\\text{th}$\" width=\"23\" height=\"15\" /> number is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/4/c74196e240998fa1f30bc151e4b4cbdb633772b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+n-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"13\" />.  We know that the sum of the group of numbers is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e59e2c6e83eb78cca610a5fd4070ae01c8d4ae60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />, so\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/8/888e4e5bedfe5956ed2b875653f2ca53257710a5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{n(2a+n-1)}{2} = 100\\]\" width=\"161\" height=\"38\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/6/3a645021b6390df0191b0afb383682688c3efab3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2a+n-1=\\frac{200}{n}\\]\" width=\"136\" height=\"37\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/7/1976836b347a3efafab3f84aaaf719c47e2bee52.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2a = 1-n + \\frac{200}{n}\\]\" width=\"136\" height=\"37\" />\nWe know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> are positive integers, so we check values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> that are a factor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/3/8f37626d49b4082c9102bf930bca51277ff2eb43.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$200$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />.  Of these values, the only ones that result in a positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/3/ec37f4048b4f92c2227c9bfe79fcb7d52ab99c9c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 5$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> or when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/8/26858c2becbfe024f2a38f506fce66d56f3e0b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 8$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />, so there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/3/a431f8e7b0ff6fd392b75cce5c065035b6833bbf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}\\ 2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"56\" height=\"30\" /> sets of two or more consecutive positive integers whose sum is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e59e2c6e83eb78cca610a5fd4070ae01c8d4ae60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME\" title=\"1973 AHSME\">1973 AHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1973 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1973 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1973\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"1973 AHSME Problems/Problem 20\">Problem 20</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wik